__label__books daniels' running formula review when most people see the name jack daniels they picture a whiskey bottle but runners will think about the renowned coach and exercise physiologist at 81 daniels has had a bigger influence on training for running than anyone indeed he might be considered the albert einstein of the sport his 1998 book daniels' running formula unlocked the mystery of appropriate training paces for runners of all abilities his philosophy was simple do the minimum amount of work for the maximum payoff runner's world in one way or another today's serious runners abide by training principles rooted in jack daniels' research and philosophy and outlined in his famous book daniels' running formula running times 				 	 					 about the author jack daniels has been called the world's best coach by runner's world magazine and has more than 50 years of experience coaching and mentoring some of world's top distance runners he also won two olympic medals and one world championship medal in the men's modern pentathlon
